{"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/Request"],"title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/iatLeeway"],"title":"Type Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/accessTokenHash(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/canonicalHtu(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/thumbprintS256(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)"],"title":"Type Methods"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK12DpopVerifierO","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"title":"DpopVerifier","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"DPoP proof verification — CONTRACT.md §21.7.2 (RFC 9449), contract 1.16.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DpopVerifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The resource-server half of DPoP: given the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DPoP"},{"type":"text","text":" header a caller presented, decide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether it proves possession for "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" request and "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" access token, and return"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the key thumbprint that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator\/verifyTokenBinding(_:proofs:)"},{"type":"text","text":" then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matches against the token’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cnf.jkt"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Why-this-lives-in-the-SDK","level":2,"text":"Why this lives in the SDK"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§21.7.2 is a ten-check list, and the contract is blunt about partial implementations:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Partial verification is worse than none, because it produces a guard that reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"success.”"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Nine of the ten look optional until someone builds an attack out of the one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that was skipped, so they belong in one audited place rather than in every application"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guarding an endpoint."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The two most often missing: ","type":"text"},{"code":"typ","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without pinning it to ","type":"text"},{"code":"dpop+jwt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", any ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"other","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" JWT","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signed by the same key (an access token, an ID token) is replayable as a proof; and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without it, a proof captured on one request can be re-aimed at a different token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held by the same key.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-algorithm-comes-from-the-key-never-from-the-header","level":2,"text":"The algorithm comes from the key, never from the header"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alg: none"},{"text":" and RSA-public-key-as-HMAC-secret are the same bug wearing different clothes:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the token told the verifier how to check the token"}]},{"text":". This enum dispatches on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"embedded key’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kty"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"crv"},{"text":", so an HMAC path is never reachable no matter what the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"header says.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/DpopVerifier/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Verify a DPoP proof against this request — all ten §21.7.2 checks.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier\/verifyproof(_:request:jtistore:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"verifyProof","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"request","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK12DpopVerifierO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Request","precise